**Found it.** `[cli.js:14](src/cli.js:14)` calls `toTable(buildRows())`. `buildRows()` already gives full rows, `[format.js:7](src/format.js:7)` just drops `owner`/`slow` for the table.

Plan:

```js
// format.js
function toJson(rows) {
  return JSON.stringify(rows, null, 2);
}
module.exports = { toTable, toJson, COLUMNS };
```

```js
// cli.js
const { toTable, toJson } = require('./format');
...
const json = argv.includes('--json');
process.stdout.write((json ? toJson(rows) : toTable(rows)) + '\n');
```

Full rows (with `owner`, `slow`) go to JSON, since nothing narrows JSON like a terminal width.

No changes made yet. Say go and I'll apply this.
